  "body": "## What type of PR is this?\n\n- [ ] API-change\n- [ ] BUG\n- [x] Improvement\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [x] Feature\n- [x] Test and CI\n- [ ] Code Refactoring\n\n## Which issue(s) this PR fixes:\n\nissue #23913\n\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\n\nThis PR advances the geometry work for #23913 by landing the SQL-visible typing and metadata pieces that are already implemented on this branch, and by aligning deterministic BVT expectations with the current behavior.\n\nMain changes:\n- add geometry-aware metadata exposure in `information_schema.columns`, including subtype-aware `DATA_TYPE` handling and SRID projection through `SRS_ID`\n- carry typed geometry metadata across the planner/runtime path so typed geometry columns and SRID-aware metadata stay consistent\n- extend coverage for non-`POINT` typed geometry columns and non-`POINT` spatial index DDL/maintenance scenarios\n- keep `SHOW CREATE TABLE information_schema.columns` expectations in sync in `dml/show` and `zz_accesscontrol/account_restricted`\n\nValidation:\n- `make build`\n- `make ut`\n- manual issue SQL audit against local MatrixOne on `127.0.0.1:6001`\n- `cd /Users/moukeyu/mo-tester && ./run.sh -n -g -p /Users/moukeyu/matrixone/test/distributed/cases/dml/show/show.test`\n- `cd /Users/moukeyu/mo-tester && ./run.sh -n -g -p /Users/moukeyu/matrixone/test/distributed/cases/zz_accesscontrol/account_restricted.sql`\n\nKnown limitations / follow-up:\n- the `SPATIAL INDEX` work in this branch is still limited to DDL, metadata, and maintenance plumbing; it does not yet add a dedicated planner/executor query path for spatial predicates such as `ST_CONTAINS` or `ST_INTERSECTS`\n- a full local BVT sweep was run, but the remaining failures are outside the deterministic geometry changes in this PR (local default-db differences, timeout/service-stall cascades, and unrelated transaction/snapshot/publication flows), so this PR is opened as a draft\n",
